  <div class="wrap">
    <header>
      <div class="brand">
        <svg class="logo" viewBox="0 0 64 64" fill="none" aria-label="RISEDUAL logo" role="img">
          <rect x="8" y="8" width="48" height="48" rx="16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="4"></rect>
          <path d="M20 40L31 21L41 30L48 19" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
          <circle cx="48" cy="19" r="4" fill="currentColor"></circle>
        </svg>
        <div>
          <div class="muted" style="font-size:var(--text-xs); letter-spacing:.08em; text-transform:uppercase;">Python learning demo</div>
          <h1 class="title">RISEDUAL Python Coach</h1>
        </div>
      </div>
      <button class="btn btn-secondary" data-theme-toggle="" aria-label="Switch theme">Theme</button>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="card panel">
          <div class="pill">Built for fast learning</div>
          <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:var(--text-xl); margin-bottom:var(--space-3);">Yes — here is a working starter you can adapt into RISEDUAL.</h2>
          <p class="muted">This demo teaches Python by turning plain-English goals into a guided coding plan, then gives feedback on the code you paste.</p>
          <div class="features">
            <div class="feature"><strong>Prompt to plan.</strong><br><span class="muted">Turns a goal into steps, concepts, and practice targets.</span></div>
            <div class="feature"><strong>Code review.</strong><br><span class="muted">Flags likely issues like missing colons, print-only logic, and no functions.</span></div>
            <div class="feature"><strong>Next drills.</strong><br><span class="muted">Suggests what to practice next inside RISEDUAL.</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card panel">
          <h2 style="font-size:var(--text-lg); margin-bottom:var(--space-3);">How to use it</h2>
          <div class="lesson muted">
            <p>1. Write what you want to learn.</p>
            <p>2. Generate a lesson plan.</p>
            <p>3. Paste Python code.</p>
            <p>4. Review feedback and refine.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="lesson">
            <h3 style="font-size:var(--text-base); margin-bottom:.5rem;">Good RISEDUAL upgrades</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Connect to FastAPI for real AI feedback.</li>
              <li>Add execution sandboxing for safe code runs.</li>
              <li>Store user progress and mistakes per lesson.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="grid" aria-label="Python coach workspace">
        <div class="card panel">
          <label for="goal" style="display:block; margin-bottom:var(--space-3); font-weight:700;">Learning goal or Python code</label>
          <textarea id="goal" spellcheck="false">Build a Python function that fetches stock prices, retries on failure, and returns a clean dictionary.</textarea>
          <div class="actions">
            <button class="btn btn-primary" id="planBtn">Generate lesson plan</button>
            <button class="btn btn-secondary" id="reviewBtn">Review pasted code</button>
            <button class="btn btn-secondary" id="exampleBtn">Load example code</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card panel">
          <h2 style="font-size:var(--text-lg); margin-bottom:var(--space-3);">Coach output</h2>
          <pre id="output" aria-live="polite">RISEDUAL Coach ready.

Try “Generate lesson plan” first.</pre>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>

  


